 control  the players aren't all the same the  covers of the comic shows Beast Boy Kid  Flash and cyborg also their eyes are  colored red rather than the skin around  their eyes taking on that inky black  look regardless the meaning behind the  respective eye effects are clear as is  the inspiration the show takes from the  comic in New Teen Titans issue for the  heroes are forced to individually  wrestle with trigons power just as they  are in the season 2 premiere rather than  being exposed to nightmare visions that  usually lead the heroes to making  horrible and often lethal choices the  heroes of New Teen Titans issue 4 fight  gray skinned red eye shadow versions of  themselves in the real world one of the  more interesting moments in the brief  scenes involving Slade Wilson aka  Deathstroke in season 2 so far is when  he enters a passcode to enter his  private Arsenal the conversation between  Slade and wintergreen suggests has been  a while since lead has been home and the  scene in the country store suggests  re-emergence of the Titans that has  brought him back when Slade in winter  green approached the Arsenal for a  moment it seemed Slade may have  forgotten the password  wintergreen offers to enter it himself  but Slade insists the code Iain says  five six three nine works and once you  see the code you may wonder if it was  his memory that was bothering him or the  code himself the password isn't just a  random grouping of numbers if you look  closely at the letters corresponding to  the numbers on the keypad it seems clear  that Bay's  named Joey Joey is a meaningful name in  the Deathstroke mythos as it's the first  name of the superhero Jericho stayed  Wilson's youngest son actor and activist  shel a man is set to play him in  upcoming episodes of titans the  beginning of season two not only sees  the Titans get a home but gives us the  appearance of one of TC comics heroic  monuments Titans Tower in most media  before now Titans Tower has usually been  represented as it was originally in the  comics as a giant t-shaped building it's  also hugely separated from the mainland  on its own Island we don't get quite the  same tower in Titans but the show does  pay tribute to the comic book version  though the tower clearly is made to look  more like a regular office building than  the t-shaped headquarters of the comics  when the camera pulls back from the  tower at the end of their season two  premiere the Titans living space is  highlighted while the shadow falls on  the bottom half of the building making  it look like a tea probably the most  blatant Easter Egg who's seen in tights  in season two but a second episode is a  phone call Donna Troy gets after she and  Corey handoff the villain shimmer to the  police as her phone rings she looks at  the screen and we see the name Roy  Harper pop up Roy Harper has had a  number of different superhero code names  over the years the most recent being  Arsenal he was once known as speedy  Green Arrow's sidekick  Coulson Haynes occasionally plays a  character on CW's arrow and in the  comics he was one of the many  superheroes to die in the miniseries  heroes in crisis could this be a  precursor to ask nor joining the Titans  there's no news about such an addition  but anything's possible it could be that  Donner and Roy are dating and that's the  reason for the phone call  or perhaps Roy was a member of the  previous incarnation of the Titans and  like everyone else in season two second  episode he has news about the emergence  of dr. light the third episode of titans  second season ghost has a little bit of  fun with DC Comics longtime competition  Hank dawn and Donna finally show up to  Titans Tower  to help hunt down dr. lights but they  aren't too happy when dick tells them  Deathstroke's daughter is chilling out  in a bedroom nearby surely after the  exchange a dick visits Rose in her  bedroom and brings her a black eye patch  to replace the white bandage she's been  wearing since she was introduced in the  previous episode later that night  Rosalyn characteristically friendly  conversation with Rachel in the Titans  kitchen Rachel tells Rose her name is  pretty  me too pretty now patch has a nice ring  to it likely the show's creative team is  having a little fun at the expense of  one of the more well transparent alter  egos in the history of comics sure  Superman is silly for thinking he could  hide his secret identity with nothing  but a pair of glasses but he's got  nothing on Marvel's Wolverine who took  on the least convincing alter ego ever  in the beginning of his first ongoing  solo series while in Southeast Asia  Wolverine wore a black iPad 2 navigated  the criminal underworld by calling  himself patch apparently thinking no one  would notice his trademark hair  nice try perch check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos but your favorite DC  characters are coming soon subscribe to  our YouTube channel and to the bail so  you don't miss a single one  [Applause]  [Music]
 

